puls.json
.claude/
HANDOFF.md
# NOTE: `tests/*`, not `tests/` — git does not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so with a bare
# `tests/` the negations below are never even evaluated and silently do nothing. Excluding the
# contents keeps everything ignored while leaving the four re-includes reachable.
tests/*
# The Playwright suites are the ONE exception, so CI can run them: each synthesises every session
# in-page and reads no file, so there is nothing personal in them. The ports are a different story —
# pr_port.py and friends carry real PR times and dates as fixtures, and they stay ignored.
# Named ONE BY ONE on purpose: a blanket !tests/test_*.py would silently commit a future suite that
# happened to embed a real session. Adding a name here is the conscious check that it is synthetic.
!tests/test_weeknow.py
!tests/test_paceconv.py
!tests/test_venue_fields.py
!tests/test_race_events.py
!tests/test_calculators.py
!tests/test_insights.py
!tests/test_strava_gating.py
!tests/test_export.py
!tests/test_goals.py
!tests/test_blocks.py
!tests/test_rpe.py
# Screenshots. The repo is public and the app is full of real training data, so a debug capture
# dropped in the folder must not be committable by accident — which nearly happened 2026-08-06 when
# a Playwright script wrote its output here via a relative path.
*.png
# screenshots/ is the ONE exception: the README images, generated locally from synthetic data and
# containing nothing personal. The blanket rule above still stands everywhere else, so a stray
# capture at the repo root remains uncommittable — which is the whole point. Regenerate rather than
# hand-place a file here; the folder is named for exactly what belongs in it, so nothing drifts in.
!screenshots/*.png
